TinyCC for Ziran's native ZX engine
===================================

A subset of TinyCC (https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git, branch mob) at commit
e23dabed154a8495f3ac1ff3cc9d04fa1c207893 (2026-10-16): the in-memory compiler
for x86-64, 32-bit ARM and ARM64 hosts. TinyCC is licensed under the GNU
LGPL 2.1 (COPYING); applications that ship the engine must include that
notice. Ziran builds it as one translation unit with cmd/zir/tinycc/config.h.

Local changes, to be offered upstream:

- arm-gen.c: a call that splits a structure between r3 and the stack placed
  the next 8-byte-aligned stack argument 4 bytes low, without the alignment
  padding the callee expects, and released 4 bytes too many afterwards.
  copy_params now pads the first stack argument from the end of the split
  structure (plan->core_stack_end).
- arm-gen.c: on ARMv6 and later (CONFIG_TCC_CPUVER 6 or more), which load
  and store words at any address, gen_struct_copy moves a structure of up
  to 32 bytes through lr, a word (then a halfword and a byte) at a time,
  rather than calling __aeabi_memmove. tccgen.c leaves a larger structure
  to memmove where the target sets TCC_NATIVE_STRUCT_COPY_MAX.
- x86_64-gen.c: gen_struct_copy moves a structure of up to 39 bytes through
  a free register, 8 bytes (then 4, 2 and 1) at a time, rather than with
  movs, which is slow to start.
- x86_64-asm.h, i386-asm.c, i386-tok.h: the x86-64 assembler encodes the
  0F 38 and 0F 3A opcode maps (OPC_0F38, OPC_0F3A) and the SSE2, SSSE3,
  SSE4.1 and SSE4.2 instructions that #asm kernels use, crc32 included;
  movaps and movups no longer take a 66 prefix, and pavgb/pavgw accept xmm
  operands. %xmm8-%xmm15 parse as SSE registers, and an xmm clobber is
  accepted because TinyCC spills every value before inline assembly.
  tests/asm_tinycc_encoding.sh compares each encoding with GNU as.
- tccgen.c: init_putz zeroes a local of up to eight words, such as a two-word
  structure initialized in braces, with stores in place rather than a call
  to memset.
